pt without published research that tests it directly."],"infobox":[["Type","Looksmaxxing slang"],["Etymology","From AMOG, 'alpha male of the group'"],["Common forms","Face, height, frame, voice mogging"],["Related","Chad, PSL, ascension"]],"sections":[{"h":"Description","paras":["Wikipedia's looksmaxxing article lists mogging among the subculture's terms and defines it as asserting dominance over someone based on appearance.[1] Grokipedia describes it as outclassing another person in appearance or in a specific trait.[2]"],"subs":[]},{"h":"In looksmaxxing culture","paras":["Users post accounts of being mogged or mogging others at the gym, at parties or school, and some post 'practical guides' for compensating for height.[3][4] The term is applied to celebrities and to strangers in photos, and it appears in titles such as threads on height mogging.[4]","Wikipedia notes the wider movement draws criticism from physicians and academics, who say it can reinforce harmful ideals and link it with body dysmorphia.[1]"],"subs":[]},{"h":"Clinical studies","paras":["No studies found."],"subs":[]}],"lore":{"intro":"Mogging is common currency on looksmax.org, appearing in thread titles and replies as both a goal and a measure.[3][4]","claims":[{"claim":"Being mogged lowers how attractive you appear in a given setting.","verdict":"unknown","note":""},{"claim":"Height or face can be compensated for by other traits, so mogging can be avoided.","verdict":"unknown","note":""}]},"timeline":[],"refs":[{"title":"Looksmaxxing","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Looksmaxxing","source":"Wikipedia","year":2026,"type":"encyclopedia"},{"title":"Looksmaxxing (Grokipedia)","url":"https://grokipedia.com/page/Looksmaxxing","source":"Grokipedia","year":2026,"type":"encyclopedia"},{"title":"Mogging tallfags: practical guide","url":"https://looksmax.org/threads/mogging-tallfags-practical-guide.738064/","source":"looksmax.org","year":2020,"type":"forum"},{"title":"height mogging","url":"https://look